From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:25:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 403/488] zero_kv_blocks and the Engram lookback in Triton's
 form

zero_kv_blocks reads only the page size before its early exit and stores
int32s predicated on the page, eight a thread 128 apart; the lookback
takes a block a row and a thread an element, with the request index,
computed count and token as predicated loads and the store predicated.
Both were 0.08-0.1 us slower than Triton per call and are level at every
timed shape (runner round 5b).
---
 .../models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/lookback.py | 93 ++++++++++++++++---
 vllm/v1/worker/gpu/tilelang_inputs.py         | 45 +++++----
 2 files changed, 101 insertions(+), 37 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/lookback.py b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/lookback.py
